# Keywords

Print vocabulary lives in [`docs/KEYWORDS.md`](docs/KEYWORDS.md). The **Rules**
tab shows its player sections (HTML comments are agent-only).

When authoring cards, new mechanics, hooks, tokens, keywords, or other rules
print:

1. Read `docs/KEYWORDS.md` first.
2. Prefer an existing operator + argument over a new verb — `[Mark N X]`,
   `[Strip N X]`, `[Modify]`. Do **not** mint Dose / Envenom / Brand /
   Contaminate, or a verb for Block, Dodge, Counter, or Tag. Those are
   effects or operations, not types. Do not copy the glossary's pile-era
   `[Forge 1 Synthetic …]` lines or attribute-exclusive table onto new
   Fighters, faces, or cards.
3. A new **token** joins **X** on `[Mark]` / `[Strip]`. It does not get its
   own keyword. Do not author Shield as a resource.
4. Add a **physics** keyword (`[Empower]`, `[Pierce]`, `[Reduce]`, `[Prevent]`) only when
   the operation is not placing or removing a token.
5. Timing prefixes stay prefixes: `On roll: [Mark 1 Toxin].` Never “Whenever…”.
6. Same change: update `docs/KEYWORDS.md`. If play itself changed, also
   `docs/RULEBOOK.md`. Map print to AST opcodes (`mark`, `strip`, `modify`).
   New tokens are `X` arguments, not new opcodes. Unique one-offs stay named
   until a second card needs the same composition.

Do not mass-rewrite existing `rulesText` unless asked. **New and edited**
print uses the glossary.
